+-------------+---------------+------------------------+--------------------+
| Connect     | CUT           | 512 byte block len     | DEC                |
+-------------+---------------+------------------------+--------------------+
| CUT         | Connect       | SGI                    | SGI                |
+-------------+---------------+------------------------+--------------------+
| CUT         | CUT           | Intergraph/Sun Micro   | Same               |
+-------------+---------------+------------------------+--------------------+

However, the drive I have had succesfully worked in a 4000/300 with the
"Toshiba Std Ver." configuration.

On my 3100/20 I succesfully used a more recent MATSHITA, with out
problems at all.

>  Does my IBM DDRS-34560 4.5 Gb drive compatile with my uVAX or not? 

Best way to know is to try. :)

If it has a SCSI-2 50 pin connector, my little experience says that
elder 3100 are not so fussy with more "recent" hdds. I actually run
mine with an original Apple disk!

On the other side, if it has a wide connector, my other little
experience says that SCSI is backward compatible only from the
controller point of view, not from device's.

