In article <h97fouon21euqh2vdddarkuu7hdm0oaj25@4ax.com>, Andy Jones <andypandy00@spamnet.hotmail.com> writes:
>DIP switches on the personality module.
>
>I don't have any DIP switches on Adaptec card or Integrated SCSI card
>on Compaq servers!
>
>AJ 

The DIP switches are used to set the "base" address of the cabinet. 
The drives then adopt a SCSI address based up the slot location.  The
slot closest to the personality module is the lowest addressed slot.

If you have all of the DIP switches off, the cabinet will provide the
drive with SCSI ids of 0 through 6 (assuming you have only a single
power supply).

Connect to the SCSI cable to the SCSI connector at 90 deg. from this
DIP switch pack.  The outside connector is for connecting to another
cabinet.

