Yes, this is due to the byte count being held in a 32 bit unsigned
integer. The size reported is modulo 4GB.

Be aware that any disk drive larger than 1.07 GB cannot be used as
boot disk. Disks larger than 1.07 GB CAN be used as data disks. This
limitation is in the uVAX's firware, due to it's using 6 byte SCSI
command packets. So your RZ25 disks can be system disks but the IBM
can only be a data disk.

