Tim your allmost there!!!

the cnfg tells you whats on the system ( im sure I'll get corrected if
wrong!)

The KN02-BA  is the boot prom and its reading from the motherboard 128mb
ram, the network hardware address and a onboard scsi.

The PMAZ-AA is an additional scsi card in one of the turbo channel slots.

To work out how to boot from cd, firstly find out what scsi adaptor your cd
drive is hooked up to and run cnfg <that device>,  so if its on the external
card cnfg 0 or cnfg 3 for the motherboard scsi.

that command will show the devices on the scsi bus eventully.

mine shows roughly (missing some for ease of purpose)
--------------------------------------
DEV    PID                    SCSI DEV
=========================
rz0        RZ25                  DIR
rz2        RZ23L                DIR
rz4        MP6200S           CD-ROM

so to boot run

boot <scsi-adaptor>/DEV/bootimage

which translates from above to  - boot 3/rz4/netbsd

Hope this helps, and if your allready figured this out well done.

