There really are only two models of Viking boards, the Unibus, and the
Q-Bus.  Each of those came in one of three varients, Tape, Disk, or
Disk/Tape.  The only real difference in the three varients is a single PAL
and the EPROM.  Also, IIRC, the Unibus is a quad-hieght board, while the
Q-Bus is dual hieght (but it's been about 2 years since I've had my
PDP-11/44 open so I'm not sure).
 
Actually....  Now that I think about it, at least for the Q-Bus board there
might be a 4th varient that is able to boot the disk.  I can't remember if
this is just the disk controller or a separate varient.  BTW, if anyone
needs the manuals for the Viking boards they can be found at
ftp://zane.brouhaha.com/pub/dan

