Hiya Dec Fans

Still with me...just before I waffle on with my findings, big thanks
goes out to the following people, without your help, I wouldn't be
this far along. Many Thanks

Ben Myers
Bill Gunshannon 
Jeff Campbell
Osmo Kujala
Paul Repacholi 
Peter da Silva
Richard Tomkins
VAXman(at)TMESIS(dot)COM
 
Still not having much joy with either BA356-KC and BA356-JA, which
both include DS-RZ1DB-VW and two 180w power supplies DSBA35X-HH
and the 70-31490-01 personaility module, connecting to a Compaq Server
Intergrated Wide SCSI controller or an Adaptec 3940UW. Both these are
single ended devices. (just to fill the uninformed on the problem).

I started laterall thinking, and found out that both these devices
were supported options on the following AlphaServer 2100, AlphaServer
2000, and AlphaServer 1000 systems, Pentium Prioris HX Servers.

I checked the specifications of all these servers, and found a very
useful diagram of how to connect a BA356-KC to the above servers, and
what controllers are required.

Conclusion

The BA356-KC and BA356-JA are 16-bit Single Ended (wide) storage
enclosures. Thanks to all those people name above that suggested or
told me this!

I've been told and found out what the dip switches do, on the
personality module, so feeling a bit more comfortable, had no worries
of connecting the external storage enclosure  to a single ended scsi
bus.

Still no joy, on completing the above, as stated previously.

To check the personality modules were working (unlikely because I've
got quite few!), I connected an external Compaq System StorageWorks
Enclosure F1/F2 to the connector on the personality module.

I just wanted to check I could see devices in this external Compaq
System StorageWorks Enclosure F1/F2. This would prove cable and
personality module are working.

Success. With no hard drives in BA356-KC, and hard drives in the
Compaq External box. This proves the personaility module is working.

I then looped all BA356-KCs (30 in total) and BA356-JA (2 in total)
and connected the Compaq External box on the end.

Success. I could still use the Compaq drives in the external box.

I then inserted 15 discs, in the BA356KCs, alternate boxes, I expected
to see the discs in the Compaq storage box only.

To my amazement, for the fist time, I could see, and use all the
drives in the BA356-KCs!? I removed all the drives from the Compaq
External Storage Cabinent, and I can still use all the drives in the
BA356-KC.

If I turn OFF the Compaq External F1/F2 storage cab, all the drives
disappear.

I've tried using external active/passive terminator on a single
BA356-KC, and no terminator, and no discs are seen.

Summary.

If I connect a Powered Compaq Storage External SystemsWorks F1/F2 onto
the BA356-KC/JA it works!

So it looks like some sort of weird terminator issue/problem?

Testing was performed with the same SCSI cards, Compaq Internal Wide
SCSI (integrated) and Adaptec 3940UW.


Anyone like to make comment?

AJ





