>
>Remove the blower assemblies from the rear of the BA356's. There are
>two DIN sockets on that side of the backplane: one behind slot 6 and
>one behind slot 1.
>
>The DIN connector behind slot 6 must have either a terminator, BA35X-ME
>or a jumper PCB , BA35X-MF, installed. The jumper module is just that -
>it has no termination networks. It connects the 4 even-numbered slots
>with the 3 odd-numbered slots to present 7 total slots to the SCSI bus
>(0-2-4-6 and 1-3-5).
>
>The terminator module does not interconnect the 2 slot busses but
>instead terminates both. With the terminator module installed in
>the DIN connector behind slot 6 the BA356 presents two SCSI busses
>to the personality module - 4 slots on one and 3 slots on the other.
>
>Note that to use both busses the personality module must have two
>SCSI connectors.
>
>The DIN socket behind slot one is not used electrically. It is used
>to store the unused module - jumper or terminator - when one module
>or the other is installed in the DIN connector behind slot 6. There
>may not be a PCB installed in this slot as the terminator BA35X-ME
>was an option. The BA35X-MF jumper is a supplied item.
>
>The terminator module is not used for a single SCSI bus use. The
>dual connectored personality modules will automatically terminate the
>BA356's SCSI bus if the second SCSI connector on the module is not
>used. The termination will lift if the second connector is used.
>
>If the BA356 enclosure is jumpered for a single SCSI bus, the input
>SCSI connector is the right-angle connectored one. The other connector
>is used to daisy chain the BA356 backplanes, or is the input connector
>for the second SCSI bus in the BA356 if the terminator module is
>installed in the DIN socket behind slot 6.
>
>Note that if you try to feed the BA356 from the non-right angled
>connector the internal automatic termination in the BA35X-MH module
>will be lifted.
>
>From your description I think you are 'looping' the BA356 boxes from
>the wrong connector. Adding the foreign box at the end is terminating
>the whole bus.
>
>Jeff Campbell
>n8wxs@arrl.net


