> PCM when removed it states 16bit jumper!
> 
> I was going to ask, what do the two jumpers do?

The shelf is wired so you have 4 slots going down, the (6)jumper/term
then 3 coming up and finally the B connector on the IO module. That
(on wide modules) has an automatic high byte termination. A jumper
in the bottom (slot 6) position connects the 2 halfs together. If you
want to run a `split shelf', them you pull the jumper and replace it
with a terminator. This gives you two busses. From the A connector
to slots 0, 2, 4, and 6, and from B to 1, 3, and 5.

Another thought; where is TERM_POWER coming from?

