I remember my product the MV3100 model 10 and model 20 having a firmware
limitation in reading drives larger than 1GB. However, if the drive was used
as a disk other than the system disk, then this was not an issue.

Another limitation that I seem to recall was with backup, but I believe we
got around that initially in VMS 5.0 with specifically initializing the disk
with larger allocation units than normal. The Backup and Restore worked OK.
Of course, one had to be cautious to remember to type the correct attribute
when restoring drives. In any event
I did not think that we propagated the firmware limitation beyond the model
10 and 20's.

The above 1GB limitation in firmware also existed with the similar model
VAXstations and DECstations from what I recall.
rtt


