> > Please comment.
> >
> The problem with the 3100 series is that the firmware cannot address disk
> blocks above 1.07 GB. As long as all VMS components that are needed during
> the boot process live in an area on the disk below that border, all is
well.
> However a restore operation of an image backup, a COPY command or anything
> else that moves files around may (and according to Mr Mutphy will for
> certain) make that disk no longer bootable. In that sense there is a big
> difference between a datadisk and a VMS system disk. IIRC your system has
> RZ25M's on it. Fine system disk in terms of size. If you worry about
> performance, well you'd better have a look at a VAX 4000 then. And of
course
> you may just as well move critical files off the system disk.
>
> Hans
