Ok, HW error 36 is still "no heat".  It appears that HW34 means that "the 
fuser was hot, but needed more heat.  I called for heat, but it didn't get 
hotter", while HW36 is "At a cold start, I called for heat, but didn't get 
any".

Those web sites had heaters for $20-30, so get out your ohmmeter and find 
out what's opened up.

