I'm looking at acquiring a very cheap bare-bones API CS20 (what Compaq 
rebranded as the DS20-L). It's got a single drive slot normally, which 
can be a SCSI or IDE disk. For this non-commercial application, disk 
space is more important than disk throughput, so I'd like to shove two 
7200rpm 120G IDE disks into it.

As you can see in this CS20 picture, there is a lot of room where the 
PCI slots go:

http://users.metro2000.net/~jay/images/cs20_05.jpg

Since I don't plan on making use of the PCI slots, I was thinking that 
with a bit of hacking for screw-slots in the case, I could fit another 
IDE disk. I may have to sacrifice the CD-ROM so it can be an IDE slave 
device, but that's fine with me.

Has anyone else attempted this? Anyone forsee any issues, such as 
cooling or the chipset not allowing multiple hard disks or something 
silly? Wanted a sanity check before I plopped down the $$$. I'll post 
results if I buy the machine.

/ thomas
