Well, it's going from bad to worse, eh?

On the front door, there are 3 interlocks or switches.  The metal part on 
the left of the door has 2 tabs which are simply folds in the metal, which 
go into slots into the printer to operate switches.  This is the interlock 
plate.  The other item is the 24v interlock, and that's the one that's 
usually pitted.  The 24v interlock I'm referring to is the part that 
screwed into the interlock plate, has a plastic base with two pins sticking 
out.  Again, this is the 24v interlock.  

Now, on to the new set of error codes.  1109.0024 is a 24v failure, and is 
almost always that 24v interlock on the front panel.  You'll need to clean 
up the contacts on that, and the place it connects to on the printer.  
Also, make sure the left side doors are firmly closed, since the 24v 
interlock runs through there, too.

As for where to get a new fusing unit, I just did a quick search on 
google.com for "lps32 fusing unit", and found a few places that advertise 
fusing units and heaters.  You can use an ohmmeter to check the fuser's 
quartz heater, and to check the fusible link.  The link is in the fusing 
unit's wiring.  There's also a thermistor that rides on the fusing (hot) 
roller.  Maybe it's dirty and isn't seeing the roller getting warm?  Is the 
fusing unit warm when removed from the printer?

Good luck.

